  "caption_handoff": "Top: common SGF generation. Sink and recent historical KV condition the base denoising process, producing a clean latent block. Bottom: direct committing dependencies across consecutive blocks. Blue inputs denote each call’s own clean latent, and rust outputs denote newly constructed KV; matching shapes indicate tensor types, not shared numerical values across methods. Base reads sink and two preceding KV entries; self-only reads no historical KV; Ours reads the immediately preceding KV. Large crosses exclude sink from committing access only: sink storage, base denoising and base cache updates remain unchanged. Inputs before the shown window are omitted, and the first shown Ours call is not a cold start. Slabs and front grid cells are symbolic, not literal frame or layer counts. Other backbones retain their own base denoising policies.",
  "scientific_boundaries": [
    "Shared top depicts the same denoising policy, not identical free-running latents",
    "Gray continuation arrow ends 12 source units above the divider, not on Base Sink bus",
    "All historical edges target committing operators, never clean inputs or output KV",
    "Base also recurs; recurrence is not exclusive to Ours",
    "Sink remains stored in all configurations despite committing-access crosses",
    "No automatic KV decay, drift magnitude, learned router or cache-cropping operator",
    "Canonical figure exports only; TeX, caption and main-PDF integration are separate"
